WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.252
- He's a singer, songer, record
producer, dancer and actor.

00:00:04.252 --> 00:00:06.873
- People call him the King of Pop.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.663
- His 1982 album Thriller,
is the best selling album

00:00:09.663 --> 00:00:10.978
of all time.

00:00:10.978 --> 00:00:12.803
- He's Michael Jackson

00:00:12.803 --> 00:00:16.303
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:18.678 --> 00:00:21.886
- [Interviewer] My favorite
song on the album is

00:00:21.886 --> 00:00:23.238
Man in the Mirror.

00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:24.182
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:25.139
I liked that a lot.

00:00:25.139 --> 00:00:26.468
- That's my favorite song.

00:00:26.468 --> 00:00:28.642
I tend to hold a feeling

00:00:28.642 --> 00:00:30.834
that no matter what you do in the world,

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.391
it has to start with you.

00:00:32.391 --> 00:00:33.729
- It is my philosophy too,

00:00:33.729 --> 00:00:35.402
if you want to make the
world a better place,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:39.384
take a look at yourself and make a change.

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:40.967
- Is it hard to do?

00:00:42.009 --> 00:00:44.188
- Yeah, well, people don't
look at themselves honestly.

00:00:44.188 --> 00:00:47.439
They don't look at themselves
and point the finger,

00:00:47.439 --> 00:00:49.476
it's always the other
guy's fault or somebody.

00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:51.998
You should change yourself

00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:53.233
and look at yourself.

00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:55.233
Make better of yourself.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.949
My purpose?

00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:01.866
Oh, boy, I think to give
in the best way I can,

00:01:03.191 --> 00:01:06.725
through song and through
dance and through music.

00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:09.138
I am committed to my art.

00:01:09.138 --> 00:01:12.022
I believe that all art
has as its goal union

00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:15.029
between the material and the spiritual,

00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:16.808
the human and the divine.

00:01:16.808 --> 00:01:18.359
I believe that to be the reason

00:01:18.359 --> 00:01:21.581
for the very existence of art.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:25.560
I feel I was chosen as an
instrument to give music

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.393
and love and harmony to the world.

00:01:29.335 --> 00:01:31.767
I remember having the guys go back in

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.017
and create more innovative.

00:01:37.539 --> 00:01:40.122
This is our thing, we don't put

00:01:41.314 --> 00:01:42.963
a lot of sounds on the album

00:01:42.963 --> 00:01:45.463
that are sounds from keyboards

00:01:46.451 --> 00:01:50.534
that are pretty much
programmed into the machine.

00:01:52.472 --> 00:01:55.305
We go out and make our own sounds.

00:01:56.506 --> 00:01:58.389
We hit on things, we beat on things.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:01.096
So nobody can duplicate what we do.

00:02:01.096 --> 00:02:03.343
We make them with our own hands.

00:02:03.343 --> 00:02:06.484
We find things and we create things.

00:02:06.484 --> 00:02:10.033
That's the most important thing to me,

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:13.566
to be a pioneer, be an innovator.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.716
Okay.

00:02:14.716 --> 00:02:18.466
(beginning of "Billie Jean")

00:02:33.497 --> 00:02:34.713
- [Interviewer] What's
going through your mind

00:02:34.713 --> 00:02:36.498
when you're dancing?

00:02:36.498 --> 00:02:37.563
- I'm not thinking.

00:02:37.563 --> 00:02:40.838
Thinking is the biggest
mistake a dancer could make.

00:02:40.838 --> 00:02:42.767
You have to feel.

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:45.434
("Billie Jean")

00:02:59.157 --> 00:03:00.603
You become the bass.

00:03:00.603 --> 00:03:02.628
You become the fanfare.

00:03:02.628 --> 00:03:04.379
You become the clarinet and
the flute and the strings

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:05.852
and the drums.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.485
- So you're almost the physical
embodiment of the music?

00:03:07.485 --> 00:03:09.183
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:09.183 --> 00:03:11.850
("Billie Jean")

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.849
Believe in yourself.

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:18.942
Study the greats and become greater.

00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:20.192
No matter what.

00:03:21.606 --> 00:03:24.407
I don't care if the whole
world is against you

00:03:24.407 --> 00:03:27.082
or tease you or say you're
not going to make it.

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:29.448
Believe in yourself.

00:03:29.448 --> 00:03:31.103
No matter what.

00:03:31.103 --> 00:03:33.427
Some of the greatest men have made a mark

00:03:33.427 --> 00:03:36.153
on this world were treated like that.

00:03:36.153 --> 00:03:37.886
You're not going to do it.

00:03:37.886 --> 00:03:39.405
You're not going to get anywhere.

00:03:39.405 --> 00:03:41.316
They laughed at the Wright Brothers.

00:03:41.316 --> 00:03:42.932
They laughed at Thomas Edison.

00:03:42.932 --> 00:03:44.872
They laughed at Walt Disney.

00:03:44.872 --> 00:03:46.966
They made jokes of Henry Ford.

00:03:46.966 --> 00:03:48.263
They said he was ignorant.

00:03:48.263 --> 00:03:49.924
He didn't have a college degree.

00:03:49.924 --> 00:03:51.384
He dropped out of school,

00:03:51.384 --> 00:03:53.328
Disney dropped out of school.

00:03:53.328 --> 00:03:56.800
They even took Ford to court
to prove his intelligence.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.728
That's how far they.

00:03:57.728 --> 00:03:59.448
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:03:59.448 --> 00:04:03.276
These are men that changed
and shaped our culture,

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.026
the way we do things.

00:04:07.727 --> 00:04:10.060
Most important, stay humble.

00:04:11.473 --> 00:04:15.322
The humbleness of a child,
that a newborn baby has.

00:04:15.322 --> 00:04:18.353
Even though you become
powerful or have power,

00:04:18.353 --> 00:04:21.219
with people, with your talent,

00:04:21.219 --> 00:04:24.737
like what Michelangelo did with sculpting,

00:04:24.737 --> 00:04:29.038
underneath all that, be as
humble as a child, as a baby,

00:04:29.038 --> 00:04:32.484
and as kind and giving and loving.

00:04:32.484 --> 00:04:35.020
Never become puffed up with pride.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.327
- How do you write a song?

00:04:36.327 --> 00:04:38.111
- How do I write a song?

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:38.944
Well.

00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:43.026
If I sat down at the piano,

00:04:43.026 --> 00:04:45.600
if I sat here and played
some chords, whatever,

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.985
and said, I'm going to
write the best song ever,

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:48.946
nothing happens.

00:04:48.946 --> 00:04:50.528
Something in the heavens has to say look,

00:04:50.528 --> 00:04:53.243
this is the time that this
is going to be laid on you

00:04:53.243 --> 00:04:55.479
and this is when I want you to have it.

00:04:55.479 --> 00:04:58.010
Now I remember when I wrote Billie Jean,

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:01.676
I was riding in my car,
down Ventura Boulevard.

00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:03.780
All I said to myself beforehand,

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.613
I want to write a song
with a great bass hook.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.007
I just let it go.

00:05:12.202 --> 00:05:13.884
Several days later

00:05:13.884 --> 00:05:16.801
(hums Billie Jean)

00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:20.603
- Where did that come from?

00:05:20.603 --> 00:05:22.303
- From above.

00:05:22.303 --> 00:05:25.161
- So okay, you were singing the bass line.

00:05:25.161 --> 00:05:26.723
Sing that again and then what happens?

00:05:26.723 --> 00:05:29.004
Do you get the other
instrumentation and the composition?

00:05:29.004 --> 00:05:30.337
How did it work?

00:05:31.722 --> 00:05:32.972
- The thing is,

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:37.734
artists seems to get in
the way of the music.

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.628
Get out of the way of the music.

00:05:39.628 --> 00:05:43.795
Don't write the music, let
the music write itself.

00:05:46.244 --> 00:05:50.563
With any type of creation, you
create what's inside of you.

00:05:50.563 --> 00:05:52.492
Subconsciously, what influences you.

00:05:52.492 --> 00:05:54.325
I'm a fantasy fanatic.

00:05:55.978 --> 00:05:59.391
Anything that take you
off into another world.

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:00.224
Escapism.

00:06:02.065 --> 00:06:03.648
That's what I like.

00:06:05.103 --> 00:06:09.003
I'm not so crazy about
the reality of everything.

00:06:09.003 --> 00:06:10.971
I like a lot of fantasy.

00:06:10.971 --> 00:06:13.343
And that's what I try to create.

00:06:13.343 --> 00:06:14.903
To get away.

00:06:14.903 --> 00:06:16.977
To become moved.

00:06:16.977 --> 00:06:20.408
♫ To become moved.

00:06:20.408 --> 00:06:22.514
I think what they get
from me, I get from them.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:24.808
I've said it many times,

00:06:24.808 --> 00:06:27.605
my greatest inspiration comes from kids.

00:06:27.605 --> 00:06:29.564
Every song I write, every dance I do,

00:06:29.564 --> 00:06:32.568
all the poetry I write, it's all inspired

00:06:32.568 --> 00:06:34.435
from that level of innocence,

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:36.910
that consciousness of purity.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.220
Children have that.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.053
I see God in the face of children.

00:06:42.603 --> 00:06:46.656
Man, I just love being
around that all the time.

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:49.140
- [Interviewer] You have
something within your records

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.819
that everybody just loves.

00:06:51.819 --> 00:06:53.660
- Boy, I couldn't say.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.077
I just created it

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:59.074
and I'm honored that the
public enjoy what I do.

00:06:59.074 --> 00:07:03.157
I couldn't explain the
anatomy of why it happens.

00:07:04.723 --> 00:07:06.249
- There's a formula?

00:07:06.249 --> 00:07:07.704
- Not that I know of.

00:07:07.704 --> 00:07:10.128
Just my heart, I put my heart in it.

00:07:10.128 --> 00:07:11.295
- You put your heart in it?

00:07:11.295 --> 00:07:12.128
- Yeah.

00:07:12.986 --> 00:07:15.564
Like Michelangelo said, you know,

00:07:15.564 --> 00:07:20.127
I know the creator will
go, but his work survives,

00:07:20.127 --> 00:07:22.307
that is why to escape death,

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:24.474
I bind my soul to my work.

00:07:25.463 --> 00:07:27.071
And that's how I feel.

00:07:27.071 --> 00:07:29.825
I give my all in my work,

00:07:29.825 --> 00:07:31.499
cause I want it to just live

00:07:31.499 --> 00:07:33.642
and just give all that I have, you know

00:07:33.642 --> 00:07:35.532
and it has to be.

00:07:35.532 --> 00:07:39.020
- [Interviewer] What do you put into it?

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.774
- Well, whatever I sing,
that's what I really mean.

00:07:41.774 --> 00:07:43.747
Like if I'm singing a song,

00:07:43.747 --> 00:07:46.486
I don't sing it if I don't really mean it.

00:07:46.486 --> 00:07:47.499
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:50.634
I made this video because
Random Order asked me to.

00:07:50.634 --> 00:07:52.004
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.141
you want me to profile next,

00:07:53.141 --> 00:07:55.562
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:07:55.562 --> 00:07:57.231
I'd also love to know which

00:07:57.231 --> 00:08:00.074
of Michael Jackson's top
10 rules you like the most.

00:08:00.074 --> 00:08:02.403
Leave it below, I'm going
to join in the discussion.

00:08:02.403 --> 00:08:04.092
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:08:04.092 --> 00:08:07.592
Continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

